      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-09T16:39:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does it matter how quickly blk_mq_delay_run_hw_queue() is run? Is this function perhaps called frequently? If so, why is it called frequently? Is this because ufshcd_queuecommand() returns a non-zero value, is this because scsi_queue_rq() returns BLK_STS_RESOURCE or BLK_STS_DEV_RESOURCE or does this perhaps have another reason?\n\nIf an I/O scheduler is active, does reducing /sys/class/block/.../queue/nr_requests to the queue depth supported by the UFS driver help (31 in case of UFSHCI 3.1)?",
